{
  "_comment": [
    "Example repeater configuration for the REPEATERS panel.",
    "",
    "Copy this file to:",
    "  ~/.meshcore-gui/repeaters/<ADDRESS>_repeaters.json",
    "",
    "<ADDRESS> is derived from the device argument, the same way as every",
    "other per-device file: /dev/ttyUSB1 becomes _dev_ttyUSB1, and a BLE",
    "address AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:FF becomes AA_BB_CC_DD_EE_FF. So for",
    "/dev/ttyUSB1 the filename is _dev_ttyUSB1_repeaters.json.",
    "",
    "Only the instance that has a repeater in its own file polls that",
    "repeater, which keeps two instances from querying the same node.",
    "",
    "This file contains a login password, so it must be mode 0600 inside a",
    "0700 directory:",
    "  mkdir -p ~/.meshcore-gui/repeaters",
    "  chmod 700 ~/.meshcore-gui/repeaters",
    "  chmod 600 ~/.meshcore-gui/repeaters/<ADDRESS>_repeaters.json",
    "",
    "The application warns in the log when the permissions are wider than",
    "that, and keeps running.",
    "",
    "Remove this _comment key in the real file, or leave it — unknown",
    "top-level keys are ignored.",
    "",
    "Field reference, per entry under \"repeaters\":",
    "  key            The FULL 32-byte public key of the repeater, as 64",
    "                 hex characters. A prefix is rejected: the meshcore",
    "                 library requires the complete key for login, status",
    "                 and logout. Find it in the CONTACTS panel.",
    "  name           Display name shown in the REPEATERS panel.",
    "  password       Login password. Omit the field entirely when no",
    "                 password is configured; use \"\" when the repeater",
    "                 accepts a blank one. These are different: an omitted",
    "                 password means the repeater is skipped.",
    "  poll_interval  Seconds between polls of this repeater. Default 900",
    "                 (15 minutes) from REPEATER_POLL_INTERVAL in config.py.",
    "                 Repeater statistics change slowly; polling more often",
    "                 costs airtime and makes the local node deaf for longer",
    "                 without adding information.",
    "  enabled        Set to false to keep the entry but stop polling it."
  ],
  "version": 1,
  "repeaters": {
    "0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef": {
      "name": "NoodNet Zwolle",
      "password": "change-me",
      "poll_interval": 900,
      "enabled": true
    },
    "fedcba9876543210fedcba9876543210fedcba9876543210fedcba9876543210": {
      "name": "Dalfsen",
      "password": "change-me",
      "poll_interval": 900,
      "enabled": true
    }
  }
}
